3. Created a more robust mocking system for all required dependencies
4. Added a loading fallback for the Suspense wrapper
5. Moved the mocks before the component import to ensure they're available
6. Used React.lazy for the component import to better handle dynamic loading

These changes should resolve the "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module" error by:
1. Properly handling the dynamic import with Suspense
2. Ensuring all required dependencies are mocked before the component loads
